# scan-triage

An AI triage layer for penetration test enumeration output. It parses raw scan
artifacts (nmap XML and structured service scan results) into typed findings, and is
designed to assign each finding a CVSS severity band using a local language model
grounded in a service knowledge base. The system runs fully on local hardware, so
scan data never leaves the machine.

> Documentation page pending

## Why this exists

Enumeration produces a flood of output: open ports, service versions, misconfigurations,
authentication results. Sorting that into "what actually matters and how badly" is slow
manual work. scan-triage turns the raw output into structured findings a model can score
consistently, with the scoring measured against a hand labeled ground truth rather than
assumed correct.

The project is also a focused study in applied LLM engineering: retrieval, structured
output, evaluation, and prompt injection defense.

## Design

The core decision is a clean separation of concerns. A deterministic parser captures and
routes raw scan data into typed findings; it never interprets ambiguous output or assigns
severity. The language model does the judging in a later stage. This keeps the brittle,
tool version dependent text interpretation out of the deterministic layer and isolates
where errors can come from.

Findings are modeled at the grain of one discrete issue rather than one host or one port,
so each finding carries a single type and can be scored independently. Host and port are
fields on a finding, so per host or per port views are obtained by grouping. The schema
uses a tagged union: a shared set of fields common to every finding, plus a type specific
detail (vulnerability, misconfiguration, or authentication) selected by a discriminator,
so the type and its detail cannot drift out of sync. The whole schema is validated with
Pydantic, including value constraints such as a valid port range.

Two input sources feed one common finding type:

- nmap XML is parsed with the standard library XML parser into one vulnerability finding
  per open service, carrying product, version, and CPE identifier for later CVE lookup.
- Structured service scan results (YAML) yield authentication findings directly from a
  confirmed flag, and capture other checks as raw evidence routed by category for the
  model to interpret.

## Status and phases

In active development. The project is built in phases, each ending in something
measurable. The status of each phase is noted honestly so the roadmap reflects the
actual state of the code.

**Phase 1, parsing.** A deterministic parser turns nmap XML and service
scan YAML into typed findings. The finding schema is complete and validated with a
passing smoke test (typed, discriminated union, Pydantic value constraints). The source
parsers are being written against it now.

**Phase 2, triage(in progress).** Feed one finding to a local model and get back a CVSS
severity band with rationale as schema valid structured output, using constrained
decoding so the result always conforms to the schema. 

**Phase 3, evaluation and baseline (planned).** Build a hand labeled ground truth set,
score the triage against it, and record a baseline accuracy number segmented by finding
type. This baseline is what every later improvement is measured against.

**Phase 4 R.A.G (planned).** Index a service and CVE knowledge base, retrieve
relevant context per finding, and rerun the same evaluation to measure the accuracy lift
that retrieval provides. The before and after numbers are the headline result.

**Phase 5, adversarial defense (planned).** Scan output contains attacker controllable
text, so this phase builds a prompt injection test set, measures the hijack rate,
isolates untrusted text from instructions, and measures the hijack rate again.

**Phase 6, agent (stretch).** A single hand rolled tool use loop that can trigger a
targeted re-scan before triaging a finding.
### Goals: 
Introduce multi-processing parsing and threaded I/O.
Refactor Phase 1

## Concepts demonstrated

Data modeling and schema design, separation of concerns, structured parsing of XML and
YAML, Pydantic validation, and a deliberate architecture that draws the line between
deterministic capture and model interpretation. The planned stages cover retrieval
augmented generation, structured model output, evaluation against ground truth, local
model deployment, and prompt injection defense.

## Tech

Python, Pydantic, local open weight models via Ollama. No cloud services and no model
fine tuning; everything runs on local hardware.

